&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt; The Finance organization is responsible for the management and control environment for WorldQuant on a global basis. The team works closely with managers, local accounting groups and advisors/consulting firms for affiliated offices around the world. Staff members are expected to act as financial managers for their assigned offices/countries by assisting in strategic planning and providing financial analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking for an innovative staff accountant to join our finance team, &lt;u&gt;initially focused on the company’s operations in China.&lt;/u&gt; The accountant is expected to be able to handle work independently, perform a self-review, and reach out to the line manager as needed. The manager is responsible for reviewing, training and developing their team with a constant feedback loop, so you can expect regular check-ins and an opportunity to grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and ensure appropriate approvals for all financial transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in monthly and annual close processes for multiple corporate entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile monthly bank statements and monitor cash flow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze the monthly intercompany balances and ensure the timely movement of funds between entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review account reconciliations and provide analysis of results/variances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare monthly expense forecasts and annual budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide local accountants by coordinating activities and answering questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in ad-hoc projects and analytical work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility on working hours may be required in order to interact with staff in China&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
