&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Role Overview&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Owns the Enterprise AI knowledge library and the role-based AI education curriculum. Responsible for the design, structure, and ongoing maintenance of both, and for executing the training programs, events, and communications that bring them to investment and non-investment teams. This role translates training strategies into high-quality deliverables including presentations, documentation, event logistics, and content management systems. This role is also responsible for managing the execution of ongoing training programs and KPI reviews to drive adoption and education strategy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Content Creation &amp;amp; Management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise AI Knowledge Library
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the structure, taxonomy, and upkeep of the firm&#39;s Enterprise AI knowledge library, spanning AI foundations, tools and platforms, governance and policy, and data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain the information architecture — metadata schema, labeling/taxonomy, and page templates — so content is consistently organized and discoverable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI Education Curriculum
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the role-based AI education curriculum, designing learning pathways for both investment teams (PMs, analysts, traders, quants) and non-investment functions (ops, legal, comms, corporate).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define proficiency tiers spanning the full spectrum of AI fluency and technical ability — from first-time users through advanced/builder-level — with clear progression between levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;E&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vent Planning &amp;amp; Execution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and coordinate training events including workshops, lunch-and-learns, and office hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage&amp;nbsp;logistics&amp;nbsp;for live training sessions (room booking, technology setup, materials preparation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with business unit representatives to schedule and promote training opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize AI adoption events such as &quot;use case showcases&quot; and &quot;AI champion&quot; meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track attendance and gather feedback from training events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Operations &amp;amp; Analytics&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain training content calendar and ensure&amp;nbsp;timely&amp;nbsp;delivery of materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track training metrics including completion rates, attendance, and user satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create dashboards and reports on training effectiveness for leadership&amp;nbsp;(adoption rates, which teams are using the training,&amp;nbsp;etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage training registration systems and user communication workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with&amp;nbsp;the AI Implementation&amp;nbsp;team on adoption campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User Support &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop internal communication campaigns to promote AI capabilities and training opportunities, partnering with Comms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curate and share success stories and innovative use cases across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain FAQ database and troubleshooting resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support &quot;AI champion&quot; network with content and communication materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather user feedback to&amp;nbsp;identify&amp;nbsp;content gaps and improvement opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with&amp;nbsp;AI Technology&amp;nbsp;team to stay current on product roadmap and new features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with AI Operational Ecosystem representatives to understand business unit-specific needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Head of Training &amp;amp; Education with ad-hoc projects and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience in business analysis, content creation, or program coordination&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instructional design or curriculum development experience, including competency frameworks or leveled learning pathways.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Information architecture / knowledge management experience — taxonomy design, metadata, content lifecycle governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working fluency with enterprise AI tools, platforms, and governance concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong PowerPoint/presentation design skills with attention to visual storytelling&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with learning management systems and content management tools&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency&amp;nbsp;in creating documentation, training materials, and multimedia content&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management and organizational skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with technical subject matter and translating it for non-technical audiences&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial services or technology companies preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Success Metrics&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality and timeliness of training content delivery&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Content calendar adherence and update frequency&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training event attendance and satisfaction scores&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User engagement with knowledge base and self-service resources&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Efficiency of content production and event execution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive feedback from internal stakeholders on content quality&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who we are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Schonfeld is a global multi-manager hedge fund that strives to deliver industry-leading risk-adjusted returns for our investors. We leverage both internal and external portfolio manager teams around the world, seeking to capitalize on inefficiencies and opportunities within the markets. We draw from decades of experience and a significant investment in proprietary technology, infrastructure and risk analytics to invest across four main strategies: Quant, Tactical, Fundamental Equity and Discretionary Macro &amp;amp; Fixed Income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Our Culture&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At Schonfeld, we’ll invest in you. Attracting and retaining top talent is at the heart of what we do, because we believe that exceptional outcomes begin with exceptional people. We foster a culture where talent is empowered to continually learn, innovate and pursue ambitious goals. We are teamwork-oriented, collaborative and encourage ideas—at all levels—to be shared. As an organization committed to investing in our people, we provide learning and educational offerings and opportunities to make an impact. We encourage community through internal networks, external partnerships and service initiatives that promote inclusion and purpose beyond the firm’s walls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay for this role is expected to be between $175,000 and $210,000. The expected base pay range is based on information at the time this post was generated. This role may also be eligible for other forms of compensation such as a performance bonus and a competitive benefits package. Actual compensation for the successful candidate will be determined based on a variety of factors such as skills, qualifications, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

a3befc4e-5aff-4c18-8ca8-7f6f3d7ef77a:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Role&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a detail oriented and analytical person to join the team at Schonfeld as a Portfolio Finance Associate under the Treasury team in our Hong Kong office. The team is responsible for the securities lending, financing &amp;amp; clearing counterparty management, capital protection &amp;amp; preservation and other Treasury related aspects of the firm across all asset classes, strategies &amp;amp; regions. You will have a passion for automation and have the drive to enhance our current securities lending and financing platform and help increase the knowledge base of the APAC markets. You will be a team player with the ability to communicate effectively and work well with others across a wide spectrum of disciplines such as portfolio managers, risk, technology and operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for all day-to-day equity financing processes including requesting locates, managing borrow rates, and PB allocations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the APAC Head of Portfolio Finance and Global Treasury team at Schonfeld&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interact with investment teams, sell side partners, vendors and internal groups to perform daily treasury functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize treasury activities and day-to-day workstreams across the equities platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the continued build out of systems &amp;amp; processes to support the Schonfeld treasury platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on new initiatives in a growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you need:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of securities lending, demand and/or supply side, swap trading or delta one experience with buy side and/or sell side relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how the APAC markets work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Hedge Fund Strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter with the ability to work independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to develop and own processes end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with the ability to collaborate and build long-term partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A growth mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’d love if you had:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A major in computer science, math, physics or electrical engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience building reporting tools and analytics with data aggregation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in R, KDB, GIT, Python, SQL, Linux, Web Scraping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional language skills (Japanese / Chinese / Korean)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Our Culture&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The firm’s ethos is embedded in our people. ‘Talent is our strategy’ is our mantra and drives how we approach all initiatives at the firm. We believe our success is because of our people, so putting our talent above all else is our top priority.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Schonfeld strives to create an environment where our people can thrive. We foster a teamwork-oriented, collaborative environment where ideas at any level are encouraged and shared. The development and advancement of our talent is honed through interactions with each other, learning &amp;amp; educational offerings, and through opportunities to make impactful contributions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schonfeld, we strive to cultivate a sense of belonging throughout all of our employees with Diversity, Equity and Inclusion at the forefront of this mission. As a firm we are committed to creating a hiring process which is not only fair, but also welcoming and supportive. On a daily basis, our employees welcome diversity across identity, thought, people and views which serves as the foundation of our culture and success. You can learn more about our DEI initiatives here - &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/schonfeld-group/life/d53089e7-ba0e-4946-a70c-f47f0d548370/?viewAsMember=true&quot;&gt;Belonging @ Schonfeld.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who we are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Schonfeld Strategic Advisors is a multi-manager platform that invests its capital with Internal and Partner portfolio managers, primarily on an exclusive or semi-exclusive basis, across four trading strategies; quantitative, fundamental equity, tactical trading and discretionary macro &amp;amp; fixed income. We have created a unique structure to provide global portfolio managers with autonomy, flexibility and support to best enable them to maximize the value of their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over the last 30 years, Schonfeld has successfully capitalized on inefficiencies and opportunities within the&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: line-through;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;markets. We have developed and invested heavily in proprietary technology, infrastructure and risk analytics and continue to capitalize on new opportunities. In 2021 we launched our newest strategy, discretionary macro &amp;amp; fixed income as part of the continual growth of Schonfeld’s investible universe. Our portfolio exposure has expanded across the Americas, Europe and Asia as well as multiple asset classes and products&lt;em&gt;. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;#LI-DC1&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

5247c96313385c450a7e6b0e2c6a87c47500b55b:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;WorldQuant develops and deploys systematic financial strategies across a broad range of asset classes and global markets. We seek to produce high-quality predictive signals (alphas) through our proprietary research platform to employ financial strategies focused on market inefficiencies. Our teams work collaboratively to drive the production of alphas and financial strategies – the foundation of a balanced, global investment platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WorldQuant is built on a culture that pairs academic sensibility with accountability for results. Employees are encouraged to think openly about problems, balancing intellectualism and practicality. Excellent ideas come from anyone, anywhere. Employees are encouraged to challenge conventional thinking and possess an attitude of continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to hire the best and the brightest. We value intellectual horsepower first and foremost, and people who demonstrate an outstanding talent. There is no roadmap to future success, so we need people who can help us build it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Technologists at WorldQuant research, design, code, test and deploy firmwide platforms and tooling while working collaboratively with researchers and portfolio managers. Our environment is relaxed yet intellectually driven. We seek people who think in code and are motivated by being around like-minded people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role: &lt;/strong&gt;Our distributed platform combines high-performance storage, compute, and service layers for processing and serving massive, structured, time-series datasets - built in C++ with a distributed system architecture, real-time streaming, RPC-based data transfer, and columnar on-disk storage that powers data processing and analytics workflows.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and maintain core components across our distributed storage, compute, and service platforms - including storage engines, query and compute execution, RPC/networking layers, and distributed coordination (routing, partitioning, replication).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal stakeholders across research and engineering teams to translate data-access, compute, and performance requirements into concrete design and implementation work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve production issues - from correctness bugs to performance regressions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code review, system design, feature development, and productionization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Computer Science or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional software engineering experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong fundamentals in data structures, algorithms, and systems-level thinking (memory management, concurrency, I/O).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in modern C++ (C++11 or higher); comfort with STL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid working knowledge of UNIX/Linux development environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-assisted coding tools (e.g., Claude Code, OpenCode) to accelerate development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear, proactive communicator who works well with a globally distributed team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to distributed systems concepts (replication, sharding, consensus), query/compute engines, or columnar/analytical storage formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RPC frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-MH1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;By submitting this application, you acknowledge and consent to terms of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.worldquant.com/privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;WorldQuant Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; The privacy policy offers an explanation of how and why your data will be collected, how it will be used and disclosed, how it will be retained and secured, and what legal rights are associated with that data (including the rights of access, correction, and deletion). The policy also describes legal and contractual limitations on these rights. The specific rights and obligations of individuals living and working in different areas may vary by jurisdiction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Copyright © 2025 WorldQuant, LLC. All Rights Reserved.&lt;br&gt;WorldQuant is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate in hiring on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation or preference, age, marital status, citizenship, national origin, disability, military status, genetic predisposition or carrier status, or any other protected characteristic as established by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

028a910c8ac0fd3eadbb7310b488a7533bdd1942:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a global alternative investment management firm focused on pursuing outperformance for sophisticated clients via our Systematic, Discretionary and Solutions offerings. Powered by talent and advanced technology, our single and multi-manager investment strategies are underpinned by deep research and span public and private markets, across all major asset classes, with a significant focus on alternatives. Man Group takes a partnership approach to working with clients, establishing deep connections and creating tailored solutions to meet their investment goals and those of the millions of retirees and savers they represent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in London, we manage $253.6 billion* and operate across multiple offices globally. Man Group plc is listed on the London Stock Exchange under the ticker EMG.LN and is a constituent of the FTSE 250 Index. Further information can be found at &lt;a href=&quot;https://gbr01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.man.com%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CSarah.Salta%40man.com%7C50106c0fbadc415bae6b08dd71e5d131%7Cf771e26b93bc4bbe8f6b7cd560ce9350%7C0%7C0%7C638791954087076774%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=5iuJXx8lcIhasW1cs1O9OyY6uKEhZDGiG5RgG9UVIsU%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;www.man.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-normal text-sm mb-4 last:mb-0 break-words&quot;&gt;At Man Group, we respect your privacy and we are committed to protecting and safeguarding your Personal Data. We have developed policies and processes which are designed to provide for the security and integrity of your Personal Data. We are committed to Processing your Personal Data fairly and lawfully, and being open and transparent about such Processing. For further information on how we process your data, please see the privacy notice for applicants&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;text-sm font-normal text-light-blue underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.man.com/privacy-notice-job-applicant&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* As at 30 June 2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Purpose of Role:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on management role at the heart of Man Group&#39;s Procurement function. The Procurement Manager is both an active commercial professional and the person responsible for leading and developing a team that is trusted, proactive and genuinely valued as a strategic partner by the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The function oversees approximately $100m of annual procurement spend across Man Group&#39;s indirect spend base. The Procurement Manager is accountable for ensuring that spend is visible, well-governed and delivering real value. We are looking for someone who builds Procurement&#39;s reputation by supporting the business in achieving its objectives, earning a seat at the table through the quality of relationships and the clarity of value delivered. Communication and stakeholder engagement are as important here as commercial expertise.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will be CIPS qualified, with a strong commercial track record and a genuine belief that great procurement is built on communication, trust and fundamentals done well, supported by the right tools and technology.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Specific Responsibilities:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of three procurement professionals, setting clear direction, maintaining high standards and acting as a consultative escalation point to raise the quality and consistency of their outputs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with senior stakeholders across the business including Finance, Legal, Technology, Corporate Real Estate, COOs and business management teams across the investment management functions, providing sound commercial input and actively influencing demand upstream before commitments are made&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with stakeholders to define requirements, design sourcing strategies and run go-to-market exercises; personally leading on complex sourcing projects, negotiations and commercial disputes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage supplier relationships across key categories, maintaining performance standards and providing project management structure on larger sourcing exercises to ensure timely and well-governed outcomes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure savings are consistently captured and connected to a clear story of Procurement&#39;s value to senior management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the embedding of the Procurement Policy and controls framework, maintaining and improving Procurement MI, KPI reporting and governance touchpoints including Legal and TPRM&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement of processes, tools and ways of working, proactively identifying new areas of opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Technical Competencies:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CIPS qualified (essential)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educated to degree level or equivalent&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience leading procurement and sourcing projects in financial services&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic sourcing, category management and contract management expertise&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to negotiate large, complex deals and manage senior supplier relationships&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Man Group is a technology-focused organisation; whilst a dedicated category lead is in place, fluency across software, SaaS, data and technology vendor landscapes is a strong advantage&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appetite and aptitude for AI and new technologies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Core competencies:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled communicator and relationship builder&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sets clear expectations and holds the line on standards&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and delivery-focused&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open to new ideas; brings experience as a strength without letting it become a ceiling&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Committed to continuous improvement in themselves, their team and the function&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion, Work-Life Balance and Benefits at Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in our working environment that champions equality of opportunity. Your unique perspective will contribute to our success, joining a workplace where inclusion is fundamental and deeply embedded in our culture and values. Through our external and internal initiatives, partnerships and programmes, you&#39;ll find opportunities to grow, develop your talents, and help foster an inclusive environment for all across our firm and industry. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.man.com/diversity&quot;&gt;www.man.com/diversity&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll have opportunities to make a difference through our charitable and global initiatives, while advancing your career through professional development, and with flexible working arrangements available too. Like all our people, you&#39;ll receive two annual &#39;Mankind&#39; days of paid leave for community volunteering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our comprehensive benefits package includes competitive holiday entitlements, pension/401k, life and long-term disability coverage, group sick pay, enhanced parental leave and long-service leave. Depending on your location, you may also enjoy additional benefits such as private medical coverage, discounted gym membership options and pet insurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants and all employees without regard to race, color, creed, national origin, ancestry, religion, disability, sex, gender identity and expression, marital status, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, age or any other legally protected category or status in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a Disability Confident Committed employer; if you require help or information on reasonable adjustments as you apply for roles with us, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:TalentAcquisition@man.com&quot;&gt;TalentAcquisition@man.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;display: table; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; width: 1000px; height: 565px;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/z3YUoZQVCHQ?si=Mr5TZZZWjNlFwnEb&quot; width=&quot;1000&quot; height=&quot;565&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

c03fd1715b6f9748894fb1364748222df160188a:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a global alternative investment management firm focused on pursuing outperformance for sophisticated clients via our Systematic, Discretionary and Solutions offerings. Powered by talent and advanced technology, our single and multi-manager investment strategies are underpinned by deep research and span public and private markets, across all major asset classes, with a significant focus on alternatives. Man Group takes a partnership approach to working with clients, establishing deep connections and creating tailored solutions to meet their investment goals and those of the millions of retirees and savers they represent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in London, we manage $253.6 billion* and operate across multiple offices globally. Man Group plc is listed on the London Stock Exchange under the ticker EMG.LN and is a constituent of the FTSE 250 Index. Further information can be found at &lt;a href=&quot;https://gbr01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.man.com%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CSarah.Salta%40man.com%7C50106c0fbadc415bae6b08dd71e5d131%7Cf771e26b93bc4bbe8f6b7cd560ce9350%7C0%7C0%7C638791954087076774%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=5iuJXx8lcIhasW1cs1O9OyY6uKEhZDGiG5RgG9UVIsU%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;www.man.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-normal text-sm mb-4 last:mb-0 break-words&quot;&gt;At Man Group, we respect your privacy and we are committed to protecting and safeguarding your Personal Data. We have developed policies and processes which are designed to provide for the security and integrity of your Personal Data. We are committed to Processing your Personal Data fairly and lawfully, and being open and transparent about such Processing. For further information on how we process your data, please see the privacy notice for applicants&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;text-sm font-normal text-light-blue underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.man.com/privacy-notice-job-applicant&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* As at 30 June 2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will become an integral part of an already existing solid settlements team for Cash Equity and Fixed Income products. The successful candidate will build upon current relationships with Prime Brokers / Custodians and Executing Brokers to minimise and reduce risk for the Investment Managers within Man Group – Prematching and Fail reporting along with Stock and cash Reconciliation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Main CSDR contact for AHL and GLG whilst working with Boston colleagues for fund manager NUMERIC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collate CSDR MI stats and present to senior management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring of Prematching and failing trades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigating and, where possible clearing all nostro breaks in Securities transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving STP rates at the Custodian and Primebrokers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trade amendments, event processing, and reference data maintenance to ensure accurate representation of positions, P&amp;amp;L, and exposures in the risk management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a central point of contact for all Prime Broker / Custodian &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert for all Equity, Bond across Man Group&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all functions performed by the Equity, Bond team are in-line with Man Groups growth or contraction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the Equity &amp;amp; Bond Settlement team across Man Group&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To continually review and improve the working practices/processes of the team. Where possible automate the end to end processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage queries from both internal and external clients in an efficient and timely manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaising with global Tech &amp;amp; Ops counterparts on a variety of strategic initiatives to provide expertise for processes &amp;amp; systems, assist in testing technology rollouts, and driving enhancements to existing systems &amp;amp; processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implementation &amp;amp; execution of processes within a control infrastructure that mitigates operational risk &amp;amp; allows the business to operate in a controlled environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collating &amp;amp; presenting key governance metrics to the business on a regular basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To work alongside other Ops teams to provide cover/product knowledge (this will happen over time as the team becomes fully established)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all processes meet the minimum Audit and Internal Control framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain awareness of compliance and regulatory data requirements and ensure impacts are managed appropriately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years experience within a similar role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the market for equity and fixed income&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideally experience within a hedge fund&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills to understand a broad set of products and complex end-to-end workflows.&amp;nbsp; Detail-oriented with a control mind set&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to multi-task &amp;amp; prioritize in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication skills to be able to partner with Front Office, Tech, and Operations teams globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion, Work-Life Balance and Benefits at Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in our working environment that champions equality of opportunity. Your unique perspective will contribute to our success, joining a workplace where inclusion is fundamental and deeply embedded in our culture and values. Through our external and internal initiatives, partnerships and programmes, you&#39;ll find opportunities to grow, develop your talents, and help foster an inclusive environment for all across our firm and industry. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.man.com/diversity&quot;&gt;www.man.com/diversity&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll have opportunities to make a difference through our charitable and global initiatives, while advancing your career through professional development, and with flexible working arrangements available too. Like all our people, you&#39;ll receive two annual &#39;Mankind&#39; days of paid leave for community volunteering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our comprehensive benefits package includes competitive holiday entitlements, pension/401k, life and long-term disability coverage, group sick pay, enhanced parental leave and long-service leave. Depending on your location, you may also enjoy additional benefits such as private medical coverage, discounted gym membership options and pet insurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants and all employees without regard to race, color, creed, national origin, ancestry, religion, disability, sex, gender identity and expression, marital status, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, age or any other legally protected category or status in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a Disability Confident Committed employer; if you require help or information on reasonable adjustments as you apply for roles with us, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:TalentAcquisition@man.com&quot;&gt;TalentAcquisition@man.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;display: table; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; width: 1000px; height: 565px;&quot; src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/z3YUoZQVCHQ?si=Mr5TZZZWjNlFwnEb&quot; width=&quot;1000&quot; height=&quot;565&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

9b6485c19311d785110f5c7167155434bc63a241:
&lt;p&gt;Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incenting collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jump Trading is seeking an experienced Accounting Manager to join its EU and APAC Finance team, based in London. The team owns financial, statutory and regulatory reporting across 20+ legal entities in Europe and Asia-Pacific, with NetSuite as the group ERP. This is a senior, London-based role with a European focus. The successful candidate will take ownership of the statutory and management reporting for a portfolio of the group&#39;s European operating entities, partner closely with local third-party accountants and auditors, and broaden the team&#39;s coverage of its core European entities. The role also contributes to the team&#39;s ongoing finance automation agenda. It suits a technically strong, self-directed accountant who is comfortable owning entities end to end and working across borders and time zones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the monthly close, balance sheet reconciliations, and management reporting for a portfolio of European operating entities, including German entities reporting under local HGB and other EU local-GAAP frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare statutory financial statements and lead audit coordination for the assigned entities, working directly with external auditors and local third-party bookkeepers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile local statutory books to the group NetSuite ledger, investigating and resolving GAAP and currency translation differences between local and group reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage intercompany recharges, settlements and related reconciliations across the European entity perimeter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad EU coverage. Build working knowledge across the wider European entity book to provide cover and continuity, ensuring key EU entities are supported by more than a single team member&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the team&#39;s finance automation and AI initiatives, applying new tools to reconciliations, reporting and close processes to improve efficiency and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with group controllership, tax, treasury and local advisors to ensure accurate, timely and compliant reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned or needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills You&#39;ll Need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified accountant (ACA, ACCA, CPA or equivalent) with 5+ years of relevant post-qualification experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong statutory accounting background with hands-on experience owning multiple legal entities, ideally across more than one European jurisdiction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with European local-GAAP reporting; experience with German HGB is a distinct advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a major ERP and strong Excel; comfort adopting new technology and automation tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing external audits and partnering with third-party accountants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable and predictable availability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Private Medical, Vision and Dental Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Travel Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Group Pension Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Group Life Assurance and Income Protection Schemes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Paid Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Parking and Commuter Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

6e0e314a040e9b3683cd12163c4da03ee431ad43:
&lt;p&gt;Jump Trading Group is committed to world class research. We empower exceptional talents in Mathematics, Physics, and Computer Science to seek scientific boundaries, push through them, and apply cutting edge research to global financial markets. Our culture is unique. Constant innovation requires fearlessness, creativity, intellectual honesty, and a relentless competitive streak. We believe in winning together and unlocking unique individual talent by incenting collaboration and mutual respect. At Jump, research outcomes drive more than superior risk adjusted returns. We design, develop, and deploy technologies that change our world, fund start-ups across industries, and partner with leading global research organizations and universities to solve problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jump Trading’s Business Intelligence team is focused on empowering the firm with analysis and insight that maximizes revenue and influences high-stakes global decision making. This team develops data pipelines, supports an enterprise BI analytics platform, and provides research across many areas of the organization. At Jump, solving hard problems with cutting edge technology is our business. Jump relies heavily on open-source solutions in our large and distributed global infrastructure that includes several large high-performance computing environments, a large low latency trading infrastructure, and significant supporting infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Business Intelligence Researcher in New York, you will have the hands-on opportunity to work with all areas of the organization while gaining a keen understanding of the use of data across the firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for talented data scientists and researchers who are relentlessly curious and have a gift for connecting the dots across data sources, systems, teams, and ideas. Top talent shows up in more than one shape -- you might thrive by embedding deeply within a specific area to become its go-to expert, or as a well-rounded generalist who opportunistically dives into high-impact problems across the business. We value both paths and will help you find the one that fits your strengths.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and contribute to efforts that surface meaningful business intelligence insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Developers, Researchers, and Data Analysts to solve challenging problems, whether by going deep in a single domain or spanning many&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow threads of information across teams and systems, connecting disparate inputs into coherent insights and actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with technology teams on process design, workflow, data management, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with research and trading teams on topics including post-trade statistical analysis of trading performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broadcast key insights globally to connect the company across regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce research that educates and influences exchange decision making on market structure, product availability, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned or needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills You’ll Need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relentless curiosity, an instinct to ask thoughtful questions, dig beneath the surface, and keep learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, with the ability to link details across different data sources, processes, and departments to broader business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep interest in and passion for trading and global markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate clearly across technical and non-technical audiences, translating in both directions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter, scrappy, and creative, with good instincts and a nose for making money&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort navigating ambiguity and shifting priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly learn business concepts, internalize priorities, and network effectively with peers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering experience working with programming languages for automation tasks (Python, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of database concepts and ETL pipelining&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data analysis, SQL, Linux&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable and predictable availability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
